On Fri, 8 Sep 2000, Prof Brian D Ripley wrote:

[snip]
>      Try
> 
> apply(X = x, MARGIN = 2, FUN = function(y) ffun(y, a), a=a)
> 

I think that should be
 
apply(X = x, MARGIN = 2, FUN = function(y,a) ffun(y, a), a=a)

or even better:

apply(X = x, MARGIN = 2, FUN = ffun, index=a)

I think you may also have problems with which copy of ffun is being used
in all but the last case.  You can see this by makeing a copy of ffun in
your working directory with a definition like:

ffun <- function(x,y) cat("oops\n")

Then run the different versions and compare the output.

