Message-ID: <27CD61B9B111D211B0DC0008C72435B7012A09DA@janbebeex1.janbe.jnj.com>

Nathan,
I use NONMEM regularly for mixed-effects modeling in PK and PK-PD. Sometimes
I use also nlme. I did not observe much of a difference between two programs
except NONMEM is much more flexible in the sence that it allows to fit
extremely complicated models whereas nlme does only very simple ones. In
case of overaparameterized models NONMEM does not produce standard errors of
estimates due to the singularity of the covariance matrix or Hessian, and
this is a very sensitive test. 
Best regards,
Vladimir

