Bill Dunlap, David Smith (both from Mathsoft) and I chased down this issue
yesterday and achieved some sort of partial resolution to the problem. I
presume that they will make some sort of official pronouncement in the near
future, but in the meantime, I'll describe what I discovered.

The bottom line is that if you have installed a .First.local() function in
the system database sp2000\\splus\\_Functio (as described in the
Programmer's Guide), the update to R3 seems to corrupt that database. I have
no idea of the extent of the corruption, but the configure.version()
function is re-mapped to some trellis function.

The work-around that I discovered is to install S-PLUS in a clean directory,
upgrade to R2 and R3, and then re-install the .First.local().

Thanks to Bill and David for their prompt replies and attention to this
problem.

