[I'd been holding off posting this until I could update the FAQ page, and it
seems David got in first :).]

Thanks to David providing us with a clear example of how to reproduce his
problem with the R3 service release, we've been able to determine the cause.

David had followed the procedure on p762 of the Programmer's Guide to add a
function .First.local to system database 2.  As the Note on p761 obliquely
suggests, if you have made changes to the system databases you will need to
re-install S-PLUS before the patch can be used.

Provided you have not modified any of the system databases (this is not
recommended, and you are very unlikely to have done so unless you have
followed the suggestions of p762), the patch works successfully.

As a reminder, Frequently Asked Questions about the Service Release 3 are on
our website at http://www.splus.com/resources/download/spls2000r3FAQ.htm.

