From rgilliam at grci.com  Thu Sep 14 21:11:55 2000
From: rgilliam at grci.com (Gilliam, Reid)
Date: Thu, 14 Sep 2000 17:11:55 -0400
Subject: [S] SUMMARY: factor variable handling in SAS and S-PLUS
Message-ID: <09A65DF294F8D311AAB000105A02DBAF3291D3@thumper.va.grci.com>

Many thanks to Frank Harrell Jr. and Tom Richards who gave the same helpful
response to my query!

In S+ just do options(contrasts=c('contr.treatment','contr.poly')).
The first level of factor variables will be the reference cell.
In S+ you should never have to made dummy variables or interaction
effects.

To have SAS make dummies for you use PROC GENMOD or PROC LIFEREG
rather than PROC LOGISTIC; use a CLASS variable.

Thanks guys!!!

