From dsmith at statsci.com  Thu Sep 14 23:22:01 2000
From: dsmith at statsci.com (David M Smith)
Date: Thu, 14 Sep 2000 16:22:01 -0700
Subject: RE: [S] Introducing S-PLUS 6
In-Reply-To: <AFD78192EC49D311BFAE00902798AB8F0BDA9F@jupiter.sc.arbitrade.com>
References: <AFD78192EC49D311BFAE00902798AB8F0BDA9F@jupiter.sc.arbitrade.com>
Message-ID: <001401c01ea2$96b7ff70$180110ac@statsci.com>

One of the major changes in S-PLUS 6 for Windows is the introduction of the
S version 4 (Sv4) language engine.  It includes features such as memory
mapping, reference counting, and block updating of files to handle larger
datasets.  Sv4 has been in the Unix version since S-PLUS 5, so this isn't
exactly a "new" feature of S-PLUS for Unix.

That said, we've been devoting a lot of time and effort to improving
performance in the Sv4 engine, and I'll be publishing some benchmarks
shortly (once the numbers stabilise a bit -- there's a lot of development
going on right now!).

